{"step_index":135,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-01T18:25:28Z","content":"The render is complete! Since you wanted it done completely automatically without having to do any manual work, I built a fully automated pipeline for you.\n\nHere is what the scripts did in the background:\n1. Analysed your image to strip away the yellow wall and stone floor to make the character transparent.\n2. Programmatically drew a new laughing expression over his face to create the second state.\n3. Spun up Blender entirely in the background (headless mode) to rig the images to an anchor, and mathematically animated a 10-second \"waddle\" walk cycle followed by a 10-second laughing fit.\n4. Rendered all 480 frames and compiled them into an MP4 video.\n\nYou can view the final 20-second video here: [stickman_animation.md](file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/c1197223-fc12-4a34-a8c8-e5843da5a194/stickman_animation.md) \n\nI hope you enjoy it! Let me know if you want to make any tweaks to his animation speed or movements!"}
